  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commonwealth Parliamentary Good Governance Project &#x2013; Phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Delivered by the Commonwealth Parliamentary Association (CPA).

Effective parliaments are the linchpin of good governance. This project will ensure legislatures can function to their maximum potential. The project will seek to ensure parliaments can vigorously scrutinise and hold the executive accountable, produce robust, high-quality legislation, and provide adequate services and resources needed to enable parliamentarians to represent their communities.  

By supporting parliaments to undertake Benchmark self-assessments (activities) and producing reports and accompanying recommendations (outputs), such institutions and their leadership will be able to identify clear roadmaps for effective and targeted reforms (outcomes). The CPA, through FCDO funding, will continue to be able to support these parliaments to fulfil recommendations through Technical Assistance Programmes (outputs), for example updating rules of procedure, training, developing corporate policies and plans (activities) and increasing public outreach and engagement. Collectively, these outputs will bring about the project objective (purpose) to strengthen parliamentary institutions for improved good governance and democracy across the Commonwealth.</narrative>
  </description>
